# Security

## Secrets

- Never hardcode API keys, tokens, passwords, or secrets in source code
- Never commit secrets — use `--dart-define` or environment variables
- No secrets in `packages/config` source — only URLs and feature flags

## Logging

- Never log sensitive data (tokens, passwords, PII) — not even at debug level
- Disable `LoggingInterceptor` verbose output in release builds (`kReleaseMode`)
- No `print()` statements with sensitive data

## Storage

- Sensitive data: `flutter_secure_storage` via `packages/storage` `SecureTokenStorage`
- Never store tokens in `SharedPreferences` or unencrypted Hive
- Token storage: `SecureTokenStorage` from `packages/storage` only

## Network

- SSL pinning configured in `packages/network` — do not disable without explicit instruction
- Never use `badCertificateCallback` that returns `true`
- Bearer tokens injected only by `AuthInterceptor` — never manually in features
- Never expose `DioException` or raw HTTP errors to presentation layer

## OWASP Mobile

Keep in mind when reviewing:
- M1: Improper credential usage
- M2: Inadequate supply chain security
- M9: Insecure data storage
